r (let dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++)` / `for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++)` with a single `for (const [dx, dy] of NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS)`. This also eliminated the `if (dx === 0 && dy === 0) continue;` skip-self conditional. The \"neighborhood\" is now a declarative table of 8 offsets rather than procedural arithmetic.\n\n2. **Extracted `toKey` / `fromKey` helpers** — Removed three duplicated `\\`${x},${y}\\`` template literals and the inline `key.split(\",\").map(Number)` decode. The cell↔string encoding now has a single source of truth, and the `nx`/`ny` destructuring bindings are absorbed inside `fromKey`.\n\n3. **Renamed `neighborCounts` → `counts`** (local abbreviation) and dropped braces around the single-statement `if` bodies — purely cosmetic, matches the existing style.\n\n**Mass Change:** ~125 → ~86 (~31% reduction)\n\n| Component   | Before | After |\n|-------------|--------|-------|\n| Constants   | ~14    | ~13   |\n| Bindings    | ~16    | ~13   |\n| Invocations | ~18    | ~16   |\n| Conditionals| ~40    | 24    |\n| Loops       | ~25    | 20    |\n| Assignments | 12     | 0     |\n| **Total**   | **~125** | **~86** |\n\nMain mass savings came from eliminating the two nested `for` loops (with their bounds, increments, and self-skip conditional) and consolidating the duplicated key-encoding templates. The `toKey`/`fromKey` helpers added 2 bindings but paid for themselves by absorbing 3 template literals, 1 split/map/Number invocation chain, and 2 destructure bindings.\n\n**Tests:** All 5 passing — TypeScript compiles cleanly.\n\n**Rule Application:**\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass):** ✓ verified\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** neighborhood is now declarative (`NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS`); encoding/decoding is named\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication):** key encoding consolidated into `toKey`/`fromKey`\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** removed inner `for` loops, the self-skip conditional, the `nx`/`ny` bindings"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3