es (underpopulation).\n *   2. Any live cell with 2 or 3 live neighbours lives on (survival).\n *   3. Any live cell with more than 3 live neighbours dies (overpopulation).\n *   4. Any dead cell with exactly 3 live neighbours becomes alive (reproduction).\n *\n * Equivalently, a cell is alive in the next generation iff it has exactly 3\n * live neighbours, or it was already alive with exactly 2.\n *\n * @param cells The set of live cells in the current generation.\n * @returns The set of live cells in the next generation.\n */\nexport function nextGeneration(cells: Cell[]): Cell[] {\n  const live = new Set(cells.map(toKey));\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n\n  for (const [x, y] of cells) {\n    for (const [dx, dy] of NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS) {\n      const key = `${x + dx},${y + dy}`;\n      counts.set(key, (counts.get(key) ?? 0) + 1);\n    }\n  }\n\n  const next: Cell[] = [];\n  for (const [key, count] of counts) {\n    const wasAlive = live.has(key);\n    if (count === 3 || (count === 2 && wasAlive)) {\n      next.push(fromKey(key));\n    }\n  }\n  return next;\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784973914759},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent refactor! Now Test 8: L-shape → block (Rule 4 reproduction)","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now Test 8: L-shape → block (Rule 4 reproduction)"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2f7b75a9f4e54e58b459b472","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"  it(\"should reproduce when L-shape becomes block -- Rule 4: dead cell with 3 neighbors born\", () => {\n    // Spec example for Rule 4:\n    // Gen 0: [(0,0),(1,0),(0,1)]  (L-shape)\n    // Gen 1: [(0,0),(1,0),(0,1),(1,1)] (block; (1,1) is born with 3 neighbours)\n    const lShape: Array<[number, number]> = [[0, 0], [1, 0], [0, 1]];\n    const block: Array<[number, number]> = [[0, 0], [1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 1]];\n    expect(nextGeneration(lShape).sort()).toEqual(block.sort());\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should 